  "text": "An often-overlooked group of laborers, gravediggers have a reputation for being as quiet and grim as their workplace. They're usually strong and tough from their long hours of backbreaking labor, and they tend to have a unique perspective on life and death.\n\n---\nSociety is built upon the backs of laborers."
